          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾವಿಕ — nāvika — \"a sailor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನನ್ನ ಅಜ್ಜ ಹಡಗಿನಲ್ಲಿ ನಾವಿಕರಾಗಿದ್ದರು. nanna ajja haḍaginalli nāvikarāgiddaru. My grandfather was a sailor on a ship."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ನಾವಿಕರು, nāvikaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on Sanskrit nau, a boat, with -ಇಕ, one who works with it: the one who works the boat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾವಿಕ (nāvika) is borrowed from Sanskrit nāvika, \"a sailor, a helmsman\" (CDIAL 7082), from nau, \"a boat\"."
            }
